VALUES ('INVH','bear_case','editorial_analysis','Demand for single-family rental homes, property operations, leasing, renovations, resident services, and institutional housing investment can slow, shift, or become less profitable even when the broader market continues to grow. Vacancy, churn, customer consolidation, or property obsolescence can reduce cash flow. Leverage and maturities expose owners to rates and capital-market availability. Accounting earnings can overstate owner economics when working capital, capital spending, acquisitions, stock compensation, debt, leases, or dilution absorb cash.','Preserves the skeptical interpretation as a sourced, reviewable claim.','INVH SEC filing library','https://www.sec.gov/edgar/browse/?CIK=0001687229&owner=exclude','The issuer record provides INVITATION HOMES INC''s filing history, including annual, quarterly, current, proxy, ownership, and registration disclosures.','2026-08-02','published','Founding editorial research',CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,CURRENT_TIMESTAMP)
